# No Absolute Paths in Documentation

**Rule:** All file paths in documentation in unified-trading-codex and unified-trading-pm must be workspace-relative. Absolute paths are never acceptable.

## Forbidden patterns

- `/Users/...` — developer home directories
- `/home/...` — Linux home directories
- `/data/...` — mounted data drives
- `$HOME/...` — home directory variable
- `$UNIFIED_TRADING_WORKSPACE_ROOT/...` — use workspace-relative paths instead

## Correct pattern

Use paths relative to the workspace root:

```markdown
# BAD
cd /Users/ikennaigboaka/Documents/repos/unified-trading-system-repos/instruments-service

# GOOD
cd instruments-service

# BAD
python /data/Upwork/On\ Going/Ikenna/market-tick-data-service/scripts/validate.py

# GOOD
python market-tick-data-service/scripts/validate.py
```

## Rationale

Absolute paths make documentation machine-specific and stale the moment they are written. Any developer or agent running the same command will get errors unless they happen to have the identical path structure.

See: `unified-trading-codex/13-codex-governance/SSOT-BOUNDARY.md` for the full governance rules.
